{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "note-main",
      "type": "canvas_note",
      "position": { "x": -10, "y": -160 },
      "style": { "width": 1260, "height": 135 },
      "width": 1260,
      "height": 135,
      "data": {
        "label": "Note",
        "params": {
          "color_index": 4,
          "text": "**CLIP Zero-Shot Classification** — OpenAI CLIP (ViT backbone) encodes images and text in a shared latent space. No training, no fine-tuning.\n\n**Mode 1 — Classification:** Edit the *Labels* param (comma-separated text) → CLIP returns the best matching label + probability scores over all candidates.\n**Mode 2 — Embedding:** Connect the `embedding` output (512d L2-normalized vector) downstream to a distance node, K-Means, or similarity search.\n\n**First run:** ViT-B/32 downloads ~600 MB; ViT-L/14 ~2 GB. A HuggingFace token is only required for private repos.\n**Tip:** Describe precisely — *\"elderly man outdoors in winter\"* beats *\"person\"*. CLIP reads natural language, not just category names."
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-labels",
      "type": "canvas_note",
      "position": { "x": 316, "y": 75 },
      "style": { "width": 258, "height": 115 },
      "width": 258,
      "height": 115,
      "data": {
        "label": "Note",
        "params": {
          "color_index": 2,
          "text": "**Adapting labels to your image**\nEdit *Labels (comma-separated)* to match what you expect in the scene.\n\nExamples:\n- Natural scene → `forest, field, ocean, mountain, desert, city`\n- Medical → `normal tissue, tumor, artifact, necrosis`\n- Sentinel-2 → `water, cloud, vegetation, bare soil, urban`"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "note-embed",
      "type": "canvas_note",
      "position": { "x": 862, "y": 75 },
      "style": { "width": 370, "height": 115 },
      "width": 370,
      "height": 115,
      "data": {
        "label": "Note",
        "params": {
          "color_index": 5,
          "text": "**Embedding output — downstream uses**\nThe 512d vector is L2-normalized (cosine similarity = dot product).\n\n→ **Similarity search**: compute `embedding_A · embedding_B` (python node)\n→ **Clustering**: feed a batch of embeddings to K-Means\n→ **Retrieval**: store embeddings in a list, rank by dot product at query time"
        }
      }
    },
